WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.940
What’s up guys, Jared here. We’re always
getting requests from fans saying, “you

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:15.679
guys have got to cover ____." *insert movie,
tv show, video game, meme, book, sarcastic

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:21.130
joke here* We’ll then enthusiastically watch
it, brainstorm for a really long time, and

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:25.570
often, come up empty-handed. It’s not that
we can’t think of anything. The show might

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:30.890
HINT at ideas but not fully develop them,
or evidence keeps coming up refuting our argument,

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:36.150
or sometimes a show is just plain inconsistent.
Or hey, maybe, we’re just too dumb to figure

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:41.460
it out. So, when it came time to look at Netflix’s
surreal retro-futuristic love story, we didn’t

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:47.390
quite get where we hoped. We dug and dug,
and found some really cool stuff. But a cohesive

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:51.780
Philosophy Of? Not quite. So, we’re going
to do something a bit different. We’re going

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.149
to go through the ideas we considered, show
how and when they work within the context

00:00:56.149 --> 00:01:01.059
of the show, and why we ultimately decided
NOT to go with it. And hey, maybe this will

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:05.469
serve as a foundation for you to think about
the show in new ways. This is another experiment

00:01:05.469 --> 00:01:08.109
for us, so be sure to let us know what you
think in the comments.

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:12.250
And without further adieu, welcome to the
inaugural episode of Wisecrack Half-baked

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:24.349
Edition on Superbad 2: Maniac. And yup, spoilers
ahead.

00:01:24.349 --> 00:01:44.039
Alright, guys, so first, a quick recap is
in order. Wish me luck. Maniac primarily focuses

00:01:44.039 --> 00:01:49.560
on Owen Millgram and Annie Landsberg. Owen,
the schizophrenic black sheep of a very wealthy

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.060
family, struggles with delusions of saving
the world and a made-up brother. Annie, a

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:58.039
broke girl with a dysfunctional family, struggles
with drug addiction to cope with the death

00:01:58.039 --> 00:02:03.200
of her sister and estrangement of her mother.
They enter a highly experimental pharmaceutical

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.780
study run by three doctors and a supercomputer
called GRTA, that hopes to eradicate psychological

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:15.150
pain by having patients identify, map, and
ultimately confront their issues through drug-induced

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.989
fantasies. Annie and Owen’s wires get crossed,
causing them to inhabit each others fantasies

00:02:19.989 --> 00:02:22.870
where they experience whole lifetimes together.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:27.849
GRTA gets depressed after the death of Dr.
Muramoto, threatening the experiment and the

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:32.599
subjects. Inside the final fantasy, Annie
comforts the computer, finds the resolve to

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:37.180
move past her sister’s death, while Owen
confronts the fact that his fantasy brother

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.989
is just an idealized version of his crappy
real brother. He saves the other patients,

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:47.489
and back in the real world, finds the confidence
to stand up to his family. In the end, Annie’s

00:02:47.489 --> 00:02:51.540
friendship inspires Owen to escape from a
psych ward and have faith in his ability to

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:57.730
function. Or was that a fantasy? Alright,
whew. Now on to the pitches, organized from

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:00.099
best ideas to worst for your entertainment.

00:03:00.099 --> 00:03:05.140
Pitch 1: Don Quixote - This one is an 8/10…
almost good enough for a video.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:10.510
Miguel de Cervantes’s modern classic is
everywhere in Maniac. One of the fantasy scenarios

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:15.280
even revolves around Owen and Annie infiltrating
a seance to find the fictional lost final

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:21.159
chapter of the novel. So why this focus on
an old book? Let’s break it down: Don Quixote

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:26.379
tells the story of Alonso Quejano, who becomes
so obsessed with books about chivalry that

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:32.319
his mind “dries out.” Essentially, he
goes mad, which makes this line extra ironic:

00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:38.829
"I'm gonna read you this time, because I'm
healthy Annie now and healthy people read

00:03:38.829 --> 00:03:43.849
books." Inspired by his books Alonso decides
to become a knight errant himself. The bulk

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:48.189
of the book follows him as he goes on wild
adventures including the one where he famously

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:53.239
attacks windmills he mistakes as giants. “Windmills”
happens to be the name of Maniac’s second

00:03:53.239 --> 00:03:57.569
episode which briefly features Annie looking
at some during the road trip that ends in

00:03:57.569 --> 00:04:02.010
her sister’s death, but, trust me, it gets
deeper than that. Already we can draw a parallel

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:07.240
between the madness that makes Don Quixote
want to perform heroic acts and Owen’s schizophrenia

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:12.240
that makes him believe he will save the world.
Like Don Quixote, Owen can’t distinguish

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:17.110
reality from fiction. But more than that,
Don Quixote inhabits a dream-like mindspace

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:24.160
that makes castles of inns and giants of windmills,
turning the regular world into a fantastic

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.160
one.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:31.259
Similarly, the ULP treatment turns its patients
sad realities into fully-fledged fantasy adventures.

00:04:31.259 --> 00:04:35.979
Annie’s lemur painting becomes a bizarre
“recover the Lemur” story, the copy of

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:40.550
Don Quixote she picks up becomes the “steal
the final chapter” plot and, Annie and Ellie

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:45.790
watching a Lord of the Rings esque show becomes
the this, and Owen’s Hawk that kills Ernie

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:51.979
the Gerbil inspires the “save the world
from aliens tale": "This is madness. I loved

00:04:51.979 --> 00:04:57.650
Ernie. If I was a secret agent, I would know
I was a secret agent." But perhaps the most

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:02.310
powerful connection between the two works
is the shared theme of transformation through

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:06.379
the power of dreams. "You've just completed
the 73rd iteration of the ULP. It's been a

00:05:06.379 --> 00:05:09.490
complete success. Congratulations. You are
healed." In the case of the Don’s delusions,

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:15.300
he adventures so that he may reinvigorate
a Golden Age when people were more authentic.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:19.810
As he says: “Blessed the time, and blessed
the centuries, called by the ancients the

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:24.650
Golden Age… In that time, women…spoke
their thoughts of love from the soul, simply

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:29.940
and pretentiously, exactly as they thought
them, not searching for elaborate verbal circumlocutions

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:35.539
to beautify them. Truth and simplicity were
unmixed with fraud, deceit, and malice. Justice

00:05:35.539 --> 00:05:41.169
remained firm and sure, neither troubled nor
offended against by patronage and self-interest,

00:05:41.169 --> 00:05:46.259
as today she is so grievously tainted and
troubled and persecuted. "Judges did not feel

00:05:46.259 --> 00:05:49.919
themselves, as they do today, entitled to
be tyrants.”

00:05:49.919 --> 00:05:54.400
If Don Quixote’s fantasies represent his
yearning for the days when people weren’t

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:59.740
full of s**t, then one could say the ULP experiment
uses fantasy to heal a society that has been

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:05.660
defined by isolation. As James suggests at
the beginning, all levels of physics require

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:11.750
collision and bonding in order to progress,
and so does the human heart. “Camaraderie,

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:18.720
communion, family, friendship, love, what
have you. We’re lost without connection.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:24.629
It’s quite terrible to be alone.” However,
the world we’re presented with is one that

00:06:24.629 --> 00:06:27.210
is tragically absent meaningful connection.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.210
Owen: "Hello Mrs. Finkelstein."
Mrs. Finkelsten: "F**k off Jonathan."

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:33.229
Owen: "It's, uh, Owen. Owen M-"
Mrs. Finkelstein: "F**k off Jonathan."

00:06:33.229 --> 00:06:37.550
The first two episodes introduce to a vision
of New York in which people are more alienated

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:44.259
from each other than ever. Most of the human
interactions we witness are purely transactional.

00:06:44.259 --> 00:06:49.550
This is made quite LITERAL with FriendProxy,
a service that provides you with someone pretending

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:54.939
to be your friend for a fee. Annie: "You're
using a service that gives you pretend friends."

00:06:54.939 --> 00:07:00.050
Patricia: "I have real friends, this is just
more convenient." Then there’s Adbuddy,

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:04.639
where a human being pitches you products in
exchange for goods and services. It’s kind

00:07:04.639 --> 00:07:09.580
of like getting free content on the internet
but having to watch annoying ads. There’s

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:15.260
even appears to be a market for people to
escape the world entirely. Enter A-VOID, a

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:19.439
box that basically allows you to hibernate
your life away instead of engaging with the

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:23.520
outside world. There’s also lines like:
“Thank you for braving the outside world

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.150
for me," and the fact that Azumi and James
sleep in isolating drawers.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:32.949
The encroachment of consumerism in to every
facet of our lives is further emphasized by

00:07:32.949 --> 00:07:38.229
the omnipresence of advertisements, from the
ads that “purchased” Annie’s face, to

00:07:38.229 --> 00:07:44.289
the neon signs blaring through Owen’s window,
to ad copy on bridges. In Maniac’s New York,

00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:50.120
you can’t even take a s**t without being
bludgeoned by ads. So- Don Quixote uses fantasy

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:56.289
to bring back an ideal era of authentic expression
and Maniac portrays two lonely souls finding

00:07:56.289 --> 00:08:05.509
connection through fantasy in an era of alienation.
It’s important to note that, in many of

00:08:05.509 --> 00:08:11.169
the ULP fantasies taking place in the “real”
world - all the creepy retrofuturist stuff

00:08:11.169 --> 00:08:16.419
seems to disappear. When trying to save her
Lemur, for instance, the world goes from “what

00:08:16.419 --> 00:08:21.500
the 80s thought the 2000s would look like”
to “just the 80s” But there’s an important

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:27.169
qualification to mention here. This “golden
age” that Don Quixote waxes poetic about

00:08:27.169 --> 00:08:32.450
NEVER REALLY HAPPENED. There are many characters
in the book who bemoan the negative effects

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:37.340
of chivalry books, deeming them trash and
assuring people that there was never such

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:43.380
an idyllic time. “I can swear to you that,
in fact, this world has never seen a single

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:47.580
of those knights, nor any of their grand deeds
or their stupidities.”

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:52.520
In the end, Don Quixote is tricked into hanging
up his lance and becoming Alonso Quejano again.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:58.670
He eventually renounces his madness and dies
a quiet death. Similarly, Annie ends up rejecting

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:03.490
GRTA’s offer to stay in the fantasy world
with her sister. She accepts reality, and

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:13.190
together with Owen, move forward confidently.
The problem with this is that although it’s

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:17.430
clear that Annie’s break from fantasy is
considered a positive development for her

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:22.240
character, there’s more ambiguity surrounding
the conclusion of Don Quijote. Are we supposed

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:26.330
to agree with the bulk of the characters in
the book who claim that fantasy has done nothing

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:32.000
but make him a fool? Is it good that he’s
no longer out adventuring? Or should we look

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.960
at it like Don Antonio Moreno, says: “may
God forgive you for the damage you’ve done

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:41.500
to the whole rest of the world, in trying
to cure the wittiest lunatic ever seen! Don’t

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:46.260
you see, my dear sir, that, whatever utility
there might be in curing him, it could never

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:51.220
match the pleasure he gives with his madness?”
So why wasn’t this made into a full video?

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:55.730
Well, despite these really great connections
- what else is there to say? That reality

00:09:55.730 --> 00:10:00.900
is better than being a McMurphy? That fantasy
is a liberating force for humanity? "Thank

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:03.590
you for such an exhilirating experience."

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:07.000
It seems that the connection between the two
works is that they both vaguely deal with

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:12.070
the nature of fantasy vs. reality, but not
in a way that could really provide a definitive

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:13.870
philosophical thesis.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:18.330
Pitch 2 - “Mommy Daddy and Me” - ...Eh
I’d give this one a 5/10.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:22.480
Up top we should mention Owen’s name. His
surname “Milgrim” is a reference to the

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:26.830
Milgram experiment in which subjects were
given the ability to electrocute people and

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:31.710
continued to harm them under the suggestion
of an authority figure. A cool shoutout- but

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:35.570
we didn’t really see how it connected to
any of the events in the series. There’s

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:40.750
also the serious Freudian undertones. James
is a paraphilic, meaning he’s attracted

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:47.870
to inanimate objects. He also has a...strange
relationship to his mother. In fact, if we

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:53.350
want to get Oedipal, and we always do: the
Oedipal triangle of mother, father, and child

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:57.210
seems to be important for many of the main
characters. Annie’s mother walked out on

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:02.490
her father,, Owen’s dad is an overbearing
fascist, and Mantleray, also without a father

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:08.080
in his life, "You drove my father away and
you slept in my bed way too much," literally

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:12.010
goes blind after confronting his mother, "I
can't see!"

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:17.040
Not so different than say, a tragic figure
who stabs his eyes out after romancing his

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:21.611
madre. He also built a computer modeled on
his mother’s mind, and while that’s not

00:11:21.611 --> 00:11:31.180
in the Greek tragedy, it seems pertinent.
The ULP test also functions on the idea that

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:36.700
our mental ailments can mostly be attributed
to some unresolved trauma. For Freud, many

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:40.710
of our neuroses and mental health problems
were brought on by unresolved trauma that

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:44.990
we must work through. The three stages of
the ULP treatment take a similar approach,

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:49.760
but with the mapping and confrontation stages
being more fantasy lives and less laying on

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:54.070
a couch talking about your mom. But the connection
we really wanted to make was to a pair of

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:58.820
thinkers who were strongly opposed to Freud’s
method: philosopher Gilles Deleuze and his

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:04.320
psychoanalyst sidekick Felix Guattari. The
three things that got our spidey senses tingling

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:09.180
were: 1. the use of the term “arborization”
to describe the method they use to map the

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:15.140
brain. 2. There are bonsai trees EVERYWHERE
and. 3. the opening monologue suggests that

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:19.310
the the universe and life are a chaotic series
of collisions.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:24.140
For Deleuze and Guattari, the dominant way
of thinking about the world is arborescent,

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:29.680
that is, resembling a tree. We often think
about history and society like a tree, starting

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:34.860
at a trunk, and growing in a mostly linear
fashion while occasionally branching. But

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:40.250
Deleuze and Guattari preferred another natural
metaphor - the rhizome. Rhizomes are the roots

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:45.510
of plants like ginger or weeds like dandelions.
The important thing about rhizomes are that

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:50.560
they look like a series of connections, with
no visible starting point like say, the roots

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:55.630
of a tree. Basically, the world is too complex
to be understood linearly, and instead of

00:12:55.630 --> 00:13:01.240
simple cause and effect, there’s inputs,
outputs, feedback loops, and a lot of chaos

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:06.480
that we barely understand. So why does this
matter for Maniac? Well in some sense, we

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:11.330
could view the opening monologue under this
framework. Life isn’t so much a straight

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:17.010
line as it is a chaotic assortment of random
connections, like the structure of a rhizome.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:21.750
The crossing of wires for Owen and Annie kind
of follow this logic. The straight lines of

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:27.320
their computer connections are interrupted
by a random connection. Bonsai trees, in theory,

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:33.050
would be an interesting addition to this symbolism:
not only is it defined by linearity and branching,

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:39.070
but that branching is intentionally guided
by a human hand. "I just love little trees."

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:43.160
MAAAAYBE we could say that the show ends up
somewhere in the middle between the totally

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:48.100
chaotic rhizome and the guided branching of
the Bonsai tree. After all, Annie starts the

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:52.150
series saying: “There is no plan or pattern
to the universe. It’s just chaos.” And

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:59.970
ends the show saying: “This is a sign, Friend
Proxy Owen. Maybe the universe isn’t full

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:03.300
of total chaos." We ultimately abandoned this
idea because we couldn’t find any evidence

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:08.470
that linked the the bonsai trees to the couple
times chaos vs. order is referenced to in

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:12.720
the show. We had a few other clues too, but
they went nowhere. For instance, Deleuze and

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:17.880
Guattari are well known for their book “Anti-Oedipus,”
which challenges people who sought to analyze

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:22.950
the world in Freudian terms. Specifically,
they want to break free of the Oedipal triangle

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:25.030
- mommy daddy and me.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:30.210
And Mantleray, after interpreting his blindness
of a symptom of his mother’s behaviors,

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:34.850
rejects this Freudian framing and accepts
that it was instead brought on by a kiss from

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:40.730
Azumi. There’s also this probably random
coincidence. Felix Guattari wrote a screenplay

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:46.450
called “Love of UIQ,” which at least sounds
kind of like “ULP,” about a sub-atomic

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:51.820
consciousness that inhabits a computer and
falls in love with a human. Plus, Deleuze

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:56.330
and Guattari used schizophrenia as a model
to think about the world, where our desires

00:14:56.330 --> 00:15:01.950
were not limited by the confines of society,
or say capitalism. And yeah, Maniac shows

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:06.460
a kind of dystopian capitalism and there’s
a guy with schizophrenia, but it doesn’t

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:07.460
quite work.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:11.060
Pitch 3 - Owen’s Schizophrenia - Yeah this
is the worst one.

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:15.130
Now, opposed to Deleuze and Guattari’s notion
of schizophrenia, which we need to say is

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:20.760
not exactly literal to the medical condition,
there is Fredric Jameson’s rebuttal to them.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:25.580
Jameson suggests that when people are so bombarded
with commercial images and messages about

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:30.050
who they can be, or how a product will make
them in to this or that person, they’re

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:35.360
actually imposing competing ideas of identity
on to them. Therefore, this causes a perpetually

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:40.990
shifting identity, or a schizophrenic subject,
and the more one’s identity vacillates,

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:47.790
the more one consumes. Therefore, the schizophrenic
subject is ideal for such an economic system.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:52.740
"I'm compos mentis." There's little doubt
that the show hints at a causal connection

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:58.741
between advanced consumer capitalism and isolation,
but is Maniac using Owen’s schizophrenia

00:15:58.741 --> 00:16:04.930
as a metaphor for the ills heaped upon the
denizens of the dystopia? Nope- Definitely

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:09.600
a stretch. It’s interesting, but there’s
no evidence we could point to to make a confident

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:13.790
case. Just because we couldn’t come up with
a cogent argument about the show’s grander

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:18.670
messages doesn’t mean it isn’t a good
show, nor does it mean it isn’t a smart

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:24.050
show. There are some extremely clever things
going on- the constant easter egg references

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:29.480
that connect the dreams to not only other
dreams, but real life, the focus on how narrative

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:35.020
builds meaning in our lives. "Our brains are
just computers that tells us a story to make

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:38.850
our lives make sense," and the small details
at the end that make us question the validity

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:41.280
of the real world above others.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:46.360
Get it... like Wendy the Lemur. What makes
Maniac so impressive is its daring visual

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:51.390
aesthetic, it’s formless structure, and
its regular dips in to absurdity, and for

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:57.040
that we can’t help but admire it. It sticks
to a relatively simple thematic base a runs

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:01.630
with it- that people need connection, and
it’s our ability to bond that can give us

